      "name": "verify-spp-retention-purge-20260829",
      "prompt": "Verify the armed signal_pnl_points retention purge for the 2026-08-29 04:00 UTC nightly run, for kanban task t_2a2b1684 (board jarvis-os). Run these acceptance checks and CLOSE the card with real evidence.\n\nContext: server env is RETENTION_DRY_RUN=false ENABLE_DATA_RETENTION=true (already confirmed armed). Baseline eligible rows at arming: 48,141,043 (ts < now()-30d). Pre-run recheck 2026-08-28 16:35 UTC showed 48,160,305 (no deletion yet). Scheduler nextRun=2026-08-29T04:00:00.000Z.\n\nAcceptance checks (do all, capture exact output):\n1. `docker logs sycodetrading-server 2>&1 | grep -a -iE \"DataRetention|Policy (enforced|failed)\" | tail -20` \u2014 for `Signal PnL Points (>30d)` look for `DataRetention: Policy enforced ... deletedRows: N` with N>0. If it instead says `DRY RUN`, report regression.\n2. Eligible rows now: `PGPASSWORD=${POSTGRES_PASSWORD:?set_POSTGRES_PASSWORD_after_rotation} psql -h localhost -p 5432 -U postgres -d postgres -t -c \"SET statement_timeout='120s'; SELECT count(*) FROM signal_pnl_points WHERE ts < now() - interval '30 days';\"` \u2014 must be measurably lower than 48,141,043.\n3. FK violations: `docker logs sycodetrading-server 2>&1 | grep -a -c \"journey_id_fkey\"` \u2014 compare against the pre-existing orphan-write baseline (34 hits, t_79620b9a, NOT retention-caused). Report whether any are NEW after 04:00 UTC / retention-caused.\n\nIf ALL pass (deletedRows>0, eligible rows down, no new retention FK violations): update /home/frank/obsidian/quant-team/incidents/2026-07-11-signal-pnl-points-retention-fk-conflict.md with the observed deletedRows + FK count (read the file first, append/update the acceptance section with the new evidence, keep frontmatter valid), then call kanban_complete(task_id='t_2a2b1684', board='jarvis-os', summary=...) with the exact deletedRows N, eligible-row count, and FK count; include metadata with deleted_rows, eligible_rows, fk_violation_count.\n\nIf the purge did NOT run or deleted 0: do 